after registration.

226
00:09:30,710 --> 00:09:33,435
Something to note here is,

227
00:09:33,435 --> 00:09:35,940
because we're doing
registered chardev

228
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:38,785
here before we try
to allocate memory,

229
00:09:38,785 --> 00:09:40,690
there could be a
case where we fail

230
00:09:40,690 --> 00:09:42,935
